  "description": "Issue #602 -- knee-bound summer evening, from a bundle captured minutes after main got #602, alongside a v10.2 export of the same minute with byte-identical optimizer inputs. Discriminates the two terminal SHAPES on real inputs: the concave row's head_rate (median(buy) x eta_d = 2.7486) sits above the best in-horizon export (max(sell) x eta_d = 2.4778), so it carries energy past the boundary, while the pre-#602 capped scalar (2.0778) sits below it and empties the pack to the floor. Replaying this fixture against the pre-#602 row moves battery_solar_cost by 30.46 SEK, total_discharged by 10.45 kWh, final SOE 15.37 -> 3.00 and grid export 0.02 -> 10.84 kWh -- four to five orders of magnitude past the 0.001 tolerances. PROVENANCE, because these numbers are NOT what the user's system did: the corpus derives a fixture's knee with knee_kwh_from_trailing_darkness (a fixture has no tomorrow), giving 15.18 kWh here, whereas production derived 10.67 kWh forward from tomorrow's forecast. The replayed plan therefore ends at 15.37 kWh having exported 0.02, where production ended at 13.65 having exported 0.90. What is pinned is the shape comparison, not the production decision -- do not cite this fixture's figures as observed field behaviour. See #692 for the head_rate window defect this scenario sits on.",
